TwinCAT 3.1.4024, Tc2_MC2, an AX8000 servo axis. Our new axis code, called every cycle:

```
fbPower(Axis := stAxisX, Enable := bEnable, Override := 100.0);
fbMove(Axis := stAxisX, Execute := bStart, Position := 250.0, Velocity := 100.0);
```

MC_Power reports no error, but every time we start the move fbMove.Error goes TRUE with ErrorID 16931. A move towards negative positions gives the same number. MC_Power.Status is TRUE. What is wrong?

Tc2_MC2 on TwinCAT 3.1.4024. After the operator presses Stop once, our axis never moves again until we restart the PLC. fbMove then reports ErrorID 17135. Here is the sequence:

```
CASE nStep OF
0:  IF bStart THEN
        fbMove(Axis := stAxisX, Execute := FALSE);
        nStep := 10;
    END_IF
10: fbMove(Axis := stAxisX, Execute := TRUE, Position := fTarget, Velocity := 50.0);
    IF bStopRequest THEN
        nStep := 20;
    ELSIF fbMove.Done THEN
        fbMove(Axis := stAxisX, Execute := FALSE);
        nStep := 0;
    END_IF
20: fbStop(Axis := stAxisX, Execute := TRUE, Deceleration := 500.0);
    IF fbStop.Done THEN
        nStep := 0;
    END_IF
END_CASE
```

Why does the axis stay dead, and how should this be written?
